    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23065" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γῠναικ-ωνῖτις</span></b> , <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ιδος</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>women's apartments</i> in a
			house, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνδρών</span> (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γυναικών</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				1.9
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Men.
				519
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.107
			</span></i>, etc.; <i>harem</i> of an eastern prince, i.e. <i>the
				women,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Cat.Mi.</u>
				30
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				2.819d
			</span></i>; at Jerusalem, the <i>women's court</i> in the Temple,
				<i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>BJ</u>
				5.5.2
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> as
			Adj., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ γ. αὐλή</span> the
			court <i>of the women's apartments,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				17.50
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑστία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					1.312
				</span></i>
			.</div>
